    "horizontalBasis": "Exact-QID retained cathedral parent and seven current mapped part plans;western tower,eastern chancel,northern chapels,southern vestibule and small northwest pinnacle retained without overall rescaling.",
    "architecturalHeights": "Exact-QID relation16609274 and eight current cathedral/part controls retain the approximately77.2x38.1m plan. Current85m tower,34m nave roof,25.03m chancel roof,15.5m east chapel and8m vestibule control overall stages. The retained16m fact is not the tower or whole-building height. Nave/chancel wall cores are reconstructed inside mapped buttress footprints,with projected buttresses and roofs retaining the mapped envelope. Estimated eaves are18m nave/18.5m chancel,11.5m east chapel and5.3m vestibule;north chapel9.5/13.5m eave/ridge. Tower wall50m,copper apron50..53m,bulb53..63m,lantern63..68m,spike69..83.5m and simplified gold crown85m. Openings,body cores,buttress profiles,pinnacle height,metal stages and terrain thresholds remain picture-led estimates;no independent survey."
